(99,'KB-0000099','Issue Resolution related to Oracle Database 19c Patchset 46, step-by-step guide','published','external','66','645','2025-08-27 15:41:02','2025-11-18 10:14:54','Product: Oracle Database 19c Patchset 46 Summary: Instance crashes after patch. Resolution Steps: 1) Alert/trace review. 2) Roll back PSU or apply RU. 3) Tune memory/parameters. 4) Recompile invalids. 5) Validate AWR/ASH. Rules: Preserve incident packages. Workarounds: Lower parallelism. disable new features. Policies & Process: SR + RCA.'),
(100,'KB-0000100','Issue Resolution related to Microsoft SQL Server 2019 Patchset 47, step-by-step guide','published','external','67','598','2025-08-27 15:31:51','2026-03-15 16:28:28','Product: Microsoft SQL Server 2019 Patchset 47 Summary: Instability after Patchset 47. Resolution Steps: 1) ERRORLOG/XE triage. 2) Fix MAXDOP/memory & tempdb. 3) Remove new trace flags. 4) Apply latest CU. 5) Replay workload to confirm. Rules: Keep dumps. change control required. Workarounds: Reduce agent job concurrency. direct reads to replicas. Policies & Process: Document RCA. preventive actions filed.'),
(101,'KB-0000101','Issue Resolution related to Microsoft SQL Server 2019 Patchset 47, step-by-step guide','draft','external','67','75','2025-08-27 15:38:20','2025-09-27 17:22:59','Product: Microsoft SQL Server 2019 Patchset 47 Summary: Service instability or crashes after Patchset 47. Resolution Steps: 1) Review ERRORLOG/system_health XE. 2) Remove unsafe trace flags. verify MAXDOP and max memory. 3) Resize tempdb (multiple files, equal size, fixed growth). 4) Apply latest CU superseding Patchset 47. 5) Replay representative workload and validate waits/CPU. Rules: Preserve dumps/logs. no ad-hoc prod changes without change record. Workarounds: Lower parallelism. throttle Agent jobs. route reads to replicas. Policies & Process: Incident comms every 30m. RCA and mitigation recorded.'),
(102,'KB-0000102','Issue Resolution related to MySQL Enterprise 8.0 Variant 48, step-by-step guide','published','external','68','477','2025-08-27 15:39:24','2026-02-27 22:33:41','Product: MySQL Enterprise 8.0 Variant 48 Summary: mysqld crashes or stalls under load. Resolution Steps: 1) Inspect error log for InnoDB/asserts. 2) Validate plugin/UDF compatibility. remove recent additions. 3) Tune innodb_buffer_pool_size/redo log. correct binlog settings. 4) Run mysqlcheck and fix corruption. 5) Upgrade/downgrade to stable GA minor. Rules: Do not touch ib* files directly. take backup first. Workarounds: Set read_only. reduce connection pool. offload analytics. Policies & Process: Parameter deltas documented. vendor SR with diagnostics.'),
(103,'KB-0000103','Issue Resolution related to MySQL Enterprise 8.0 Variant 48, step-by-step guide — Diagnostics & Recovery','published','external','68','581','2025-08-27 15:46:49','2025-10-09 01:17:19','Product: MySQL Enterprise 8.0 Variant 48 Summary: Instability after plugin/engine changes. Resolution Steps: 1) Remove incompatible plugins. 2) Start with --skip-grant-tables if needed to recover. 3) Rebuild corrupted indexes/tables. 4) Apply fixed minor version. 5) Re-enable plugins one at a time. Rules: Preserve logs/slow logs. maintenance window required. Workarounds: Route reads to replicas. cap concurrent connections. Policies & Process: Postmortem in 72h. prevention tasks created.'),
(104,'KB-0000104','Issue Resolution related to PostgreSQL 14 Variant 49, step-by-step guide','published','internal','69','235','2025-08-27 15:49:46','2026-01-06 08:32:33','Product: PostgreSQL 14 Variant 49 Summary: Backend crashes/OOM and 5xx from applications. Resolution Steps: 1) Review logs for FATAL/OOM and extensions mismatch. 2) Tune shared_buffers/work_mem. cap max_connections. 3) VACUUM FULL/REINDEX bloated objects. 4) Apply latest 14.x minor. 5) Validate replication lag and failover. Rules: Keep WAL for recovery. no fs-level edits to data dir. Workarounds: Route reads to replica. reduce autovacuum cost delay. Policies & Process: Backup verification. change runbook.'),
