(175,'KB-0000175','Issue Resolution related to VMware vSphere Enterprise Plus Variant 94, step-by-step guide','published','internal','114','236','2025-08-27 15:46:56','2025-12-05 12:34:43','Product: VMware vSphere Enterprise Plus Variant 94 Summary: Host PSODs/instability. Resolution Steps: 1) Collect bundle. 2) Evacuate & rollback. 3) Reconcile vDS. 4) Apply fixed patch. 5) Validate HA/DRS. Rules: Maintenance mode. Workarounds: Affinity rules. pin compatibility. Policies & Process: DR drill. RCA.'),
(176,'KB-0000176','Issue Resolution related to Docker Enterprise Variant 95, step-by-step guide','published','external','115','606','2025-08-27 15:47:48','2025-11-11 17:14:11','Product: Docker Enterprise Variant 95 Summary: Engine crashes/daemon hangs. Resolution Steps: 1) Daemon log triage. 2) Revert runtime/storage changes. 3) Clear overlay2 as per guide. 4) Pin images & rebuild. 5) Restart nodes. Rules: Signed images. avoid force prune. Workarounds: Scale replicas. cordon nodes. Policies & Process: CI/CD gates updated.'),
(177,'KB-0000177','Issue Resolution related to Kubernetes Distribution (RKE2) Variant 96, step-by-step guide','published','internal','116','290','2025-08-27 15:32:17','2025-09-25 20:32:57','Product: Kubernetes (RKE2) Variant 96 Summary: Control-plane/API instability. Resolution Steps: 1) etcd quorum check. 2) Cordon/drain. 3) Roll back control plane. 4) Fix CNI/RBAC. 5) Restart components in sequence. Rules: Ticketed changes. keep audit. Workarounds: Reduce HPA. relax PDBs. Policies & Process: Incident roles. postmortem.'),
(178,'KB-0000178','Issue Resolution related to Atlassian Jira Data Center Variant 97, step-by-step guide','published','internal','117','75','2025-08-27 15:41:07','2025-10-15 15:10:29','Product: Atlassian Jira Data Center Variant 97 Summary: App nodes crash/unresponsive. Resolution Steps: 1) Review logs. 2) Disable incompatible apps. 3) Reindex. tune JVM. 4) Validate DB driver/pool. 5) Patch to LTS. Rules: Version control. backups. Workarounds: Read-only mode. limit jobs. Policies & Process: Blue/green. RCA.'),
(179,'KB-0000179','Issue Resolution related to Atlassian Jira Data Center Variant 97, step-by-step guide — Crash/Stability','published','external','117','718','2025-08-27 15:45:43','2026-03-25 02:57:50','Product: Atlassian Jira Data Center Variant 97 Summary: Instability after app updates. Resolution Steps: 1) Remove apps. 2) reindex. 3) adjust DB pool. 4) JVM rollback. 5) soak test. Rules: Maintenance window. evidence kept. Workarounds: Reduce indexers. limit automations. Policies & Process: RCA & prevention items.'),
(180,'KB-0000180','Issue Resolution related to Adobe Acrobat DC Variant 98, step-by-step guide','published','external','118','635','2025-08-27 15:49:35','2025-11-25 12:28:26','Product: Adobe Acrobat DC Variant 98 Summary: Crash on open/save. Resolution Steps: 1) Reset prefs. 2) disable add-ins. 3) repair. 4) patch. 5) rebuild PDFs. Rules: Licensing. data protection. Workarounds: Alternate viewer. PDF/A. Policies & Process: Track versions & impact.'),
(181,'KB-0000181','Issue Resolution related to Adobe Acrobat DC Variant 98, step-by-step guide — Diagnostics & Recovery','published','internal','118','116','2025-08-27 15:37:38','2026-02-26 08:16:30','Product: Adobe Acrobat DC Variant 98 Summary: Instability after plugin change. Resolution Steps: 1) Remove plugins. 2) Reset sandbox. 3) Repair & patch. 4) Clear profile cache. 5) Validate. Rules: Preserve logs. backup before registry edits. Workarounds: Use web viewer. temp disable protected mode (policy). Policies & Process: Update SOE.'),
(182,'KB-0000182','Issue Resolution related to Microsoft Exchange Server 2019 Variant 99, step-by-step guide','published','internal','119','434','2025-08-27 15:32:50','2026-01-26 05:22:00','Product: Microsoft Exchange Server 2019 Variant 99 Summary: Transport/Mailbox instability. Resolution Steps: 1) HealthChecker. 2) repair DBs. 3) fix connectors. 4) apply CU/SU. 5) validate exclusions. Rules: Compliance retained. Workarounds: Reroute mail. disable new rules. Policies & Process: CAB. RCA.'),
(183,'KB-0000183','Issue Resolution related to Microsoft System Center Variant 100, step-by-step guide','published','external','120','210','2025-08-27 15:45:40','2025-09-27 20:08:15','Product: Microsoft System Center Variant 100 Summary: Console/agent instability. Resolution Steps: 1) Patch UR. 2) Restore MPs. 3) Repair management server. 4) Fix SPNs/perms. 5) Validate agents. Rules: No direct DB writes. Workarounds: Scope discovery. bypass noisy rules. Policies & Process: Update runbooks.'),
(184,'KB-0000184','Issue Resolution related to Dell PowerEdge R740, step-by-step guide','draft','internal','121','31','2025-08-27 15:37:29','2026-01-18 07:19:46','Product: Dell PowerEdge R740 Summary: Server crashes/PSU or thermal events. Resolution Steps: 1) Collect iDRAC logs/LCC exports. 2) Update BIOS/iDRAC/NIC/RAID firmware to supported bundle. 3) Reseat DIMMs/PSUs. run diagnostics. 4) Validate RAID health & drivers. 5) Burn-in under load. Rules: Maintenance window. ESD precautions. Workarounds: Move workload. reduce power draw. single PSU failover test. Policies & Process: Asset/firmware baseline updated. vendor case if faults persist.'),
(185,'KB-0000185','Issue Resolution related to Dell PowerEdge R740, step-by-step guide — Diagnostics & Recovery','published','external','121','536','2025-08-27 15:49:14','2026-06-01 08:48:30','Product: Dell PowerEdge R740 Summary: Unexpected reboots after firmware update. Resolution Steps: 1) Roll back to last stable firmware bundle. 2) Validate thermal/power policies. 3) Swap suspect DIMMs/PSU to isolate. 4) Apply corrected bundle. 5) Soak test. Rules: Preserve lifecycle logs. document changes. Workarounds: Underclock/turbo off temporarily. redistribute VMs. Policies & Process: CAB & vendor SR.'),
(186,'KB-0000186','Issue Resolution related to Dell PowerEdge R750, step-by-step guide','retired','external','122','705','2025-08-27 15:32:10','2025-09-05 09:05:33','Product: Dell PowerEdge R750 Summary: System instability/crash. Resolution Steps: 1) Export iDRAC logs. 2) Update BIOS/iDRAC/RAID. 3) Reseat components. run diagnostics. 4) Validate drivers/firmware. 5) Burn-in. Rules: Maintenance window. ESD safety. Workarounds: Reduce load. swap components to isolate. Policies & Process: Baseline & SR if errors.'),
(187,'KB-0000187','Issue Resolution related to Dell PowerEdge R750, step-by-step guide — Crash/Stability','published','internal','122','529','2025-08-27 15:45:57','2026-05-27 14:44:00','Product: Dell PowerEdge R750 Summary: Reboots after microcode update. Resolution Steps: 1) Revert microcode/BIOS. 2) Validate memory profile & thermal policy. 3) Update to fixed bundle. 4) Component swap tests. 5) Soak test. Rules: Keep lifecycle logs. record FRU swaps. Workarounds: Power cap. move critical VMs. Policies & Process: Change approval. vendor escalation.'),
(188,'KB-0000188','Issue Resolution related to HPE ProLiant DL380 Gen10, step-by-step guide','retired','internal','123','645','2025-08-27 15:50:25','2026-05-11 20:40:03','Product: HPE ProLiant DL380 Gen10 Summary: System crashes/thermal/PSU faults. Resolution Steps: 1) Collect iLO logs. 2) Update SPP bundle. 3) Reseat DIMMs/PSUs. diagnostics. 4) Validate array health & drivers. 5) Burn-in. Rules: Maintenance window. ESD safety. Workarounds: Power cap. redistribute load. Policies & Process: Baseline updated. vendor case if needed.'),
(189,'KB-0000189','Issue Resolution related to HPE ProLiant DL380 Gen10, step-by-step guide — Diagnostics & Recovery','published','external','123','362','2025-08-27 15:41:49','2026-05-06 15:27:52','Product: HPE ProLiant DL380 Gen10 Summary: Reboots after firmware update. Resolution Steps: 1) Roll back SPP. 2) Validate thermal policies. 3) Swap DIMMs/PSU to isolate. 4) Apply fixed SPP. 5) Soak test. Rules: Preserve iLO history. document changes. Workarounds: Underclock. move workloads. Policies & Process: CAB & vendor SR.'),
(190,'KB-0000190','Issue Resolution related to HPE ProLiant DL385 Gen11, step-by-step guide','published','external','124','188','2025-08-27 15:39:56','2025-11-26 02:57:49','Product: HPE ProLiant DL385 Gen11 Summary: OS crashes or ECC errors. Resolution Steps: 1) iLO logs & diagnostics. 2) Update firmware bundle. 3) Reseat/replace DIMMs. check BIOS memory profile. 4) Validate drivers. 5) Burn-in. Rules: ESD. maintenance window. Workarounds: Reduce load. relocate high-risk VMs. Policies & Process: Baseline/asset updated. SR as needed.'),
(191,'KB-0000191','Issue Resolution related to HPE ProLiant DL385 Gen11, step-by-step guide — Crash/Stability','retired','internal','124','31','2025-08-27 15:43:49','2026-03-19 21:17:27','Product: HPE ProLiant DL385 Gen11 Summary: Reboots after BIOS change. Resolution Steps: 1) Revert BIOS settings. 2) Apply fixed firmware. 3) Component isolation tests. 4) Validate storage/NIC drivers. 5) Soak test. Rules: Preserve logs. record FRU swaps. Workarounds: Cap power. migrate workloads. Policies & Process: Change control. vendor escalation.'),
(192,'KB-0000192','Issue Resolution related to Cisco Catalyst 9300, step-by-step guide','published','external','125','165','2025-08-27 15:36:36','2026-03-13 06:18:48','Product: Cisco Catalyst 9300 Summary: Switch reboots/crashes or stack instability. Resolution Steps: 1) Collect tech-support & crashinfo. 2) Validate IOS-XE recommended release. roll back if regression. 3) Check stack/PoE/ASIC error counters. 4) Remove problematic features/modules. 5) Apply fixed image and monitor. Rules: Change window. config backup before upgrade. Workarounds: Isolate affected stack member. disable unstable features. Policies & Process: TAC case with logs. change network SOP.'),
(193,'KB-0000193','Issue Resolution related to Cisco ASA 5525-X, step-by-step guide','published','internal','126','606','2025-08-27 15:34:29','2026-06-11 18:40:24','Product: Cisco ASA 5525-X Summary: Firewall crashes/reloads or packet drops. Resolution Steps: 1) Collect show tech-support. crash dumps. 2) Validate ASA/ASDM versions. revert if regression. 3) Review SNORT/IPS or Smart licensing conflicts. 4) Remove/adjust new policies. 5) Apply fixed software and reload during window. Rules: Preserve evidence. backup config. Workarounds: Failover to standby. bypass contentious features. Policies & Process: TAC engagement. change record.'),
(194,'KB-0000194','Issue Resolution related to Juniper EX4300, step-by-step guide','published','internal','127','170','2025-08-27 15:42:13','2026-05-09 22:50:39','Product: Juniper EX4300 Summary: Switch instability/crashes. Resolution Steps: 1) Request support info and core files. 2) Validate JunOS version. consider rollback. 3) Review VC/MC-LAG/PoE logs. 4) Disable/adjust new features. 5) Apply fixed JunOS and monitor. Rules: Maintenance window. config backup. Workarounds: Remove affected member from VC. limit PoE load. Policies & Process: JTAC case. SOP update.'),
(195,'KB-0000195','Issue Resolution related to Palo Alto Networks PA-3220, step-by-step guide','retired','internal','128','170','2025-08-27 15:34:47','2025-10-15 22:05:34','Product: Palo Alto Networks PA-3220 Summary: Device reboots/packet loss after content update. Resolution Steps: 1) Export tech support file. 2) Roll back PAN-OS/content. 3) Review dataplane crashes and session logs. 4) Disable problematic profiles. 5) Apply fixed content/PAN-OS. Rules: Preserve logs. change ticket. Workarounds: Fail over HA. bypass new profiles. Policies & Process: TAC case. RCA.'),
(196,'KB-0000196','Issue Resolution related to Fortinet FortiGate 100F, step-by-step guide','published','internal','129','782','2025-08-27 15:38:49','2026-05-02 07:28:42','Product: Fortinet FortiGate 100F Summary: Reboots or high CPU leading to drops. Resolution Steps: 1) Collect diag debug/crashlogs. 2) Validate FortiOS target release. rollback if needed. 3) Review IPS/SSL inspection policies. 4) Disable new UTM features temporarily. 5) Upgrade to fixed image and monitor. Rules: Backup config. change window. Workarounds: Switch to flow mode. bypass inspection for critical apps. Policies & Process: TAC ticket. SOP update.'),
(197,'KB-0000197','Issue Resolution related to NetApp FAS2750, step-by-step guide','retired','internal','130','581','2025-08-27 15:44:37','2026-03-30 06:27:53','Product: NetApp FAS2750 Summary: Node panics/performance collapse. Resolution Steps: 1) Gather AutoSupport. 2) Validate ONTAP version. rollback if regression. 3) Check aggregate/WAFL events. 4) Correct network failover/LIFs. 5) Apply fixed ONTAP. Rules: Maintenance window. snapshot protection. Workarounds: Throttle workloads. relocate LIFs. Policies & Process: Support case. change record.'),
(198,'KB-0000198','Issue Resolution related to Pure Storage FlashArray//X, step-by-step guide','published','internal','131','714','2025-08-27 15:33:16','2026-05-03 06:47:26','Product: Pure Storage FlashArray//X Summary: Controller reboots or latency spikes. Resolution Steps: 1) Collect support bundle. 2) Validate Purity version. rollback/advance to recommended. 3) Check host multipath/firmware. 4) Balance workloads. fix queue depth. 5) Apply fix and confirm performance. Rules: Maintenance window. ensure data protection. Workarounds: Move noisy neighbors. reduce queue depth. Policies & Process: Support engagement. RCA.'),
(199,'KB-0000199','Issue Resolution related to APC Smart-UPS SRT3000, step-by-step guide','published','external','132','635','2025-08-27 15:38:05','2026-05-16 06:13:05','Product: APC Smart-UPS SRT3000 Summary: UPS unexpected transfer/reboots. Resolution Steps: 1) Export event logs via PowerChute/web. 2) Update firmware. calibrate batteries. 3) Validate load/power factor. 4) Inspect environment/vents. 5) Replace batteries or UPS if faults persist. Rules: Safety procedures. scheduled maintenance. Workarounds: Reduce load. transfer to bypass with caution. Policies & Process: Asset tracking. vendor RMA if needed.'),
